  "note": "Election of three members of the Holywood Urban Council, polled Saturday 15 January 1927 (Northern Herald, 22 January 1927, p. 8). Four candidates for three seats; the paper reports two Unionists and one Nationalist returned. M'Cavana was the only new candidate; the retiring member Samuel Shearan was defeated."
